cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  From Fragmented Alerts to Actionable Intelligence: behaviour-anchored
  retrieval for incident reporting on SIEM log streams
message: >-
  If you use this software or its experimental outputs, please cite the thesis
  below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Joel Isaria
    family-names: Mwende
    affiliation: >-
      SRH Berlin University of Applied Sciences and Kadir Has University
      (cyberMACS Erasmus Mundus Joint Master)
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/Joel89899/RAG-Based-Incident-Reporting-on-SIEM-Log-Streams
abstract: >-
  A seven-stage pipeline that groups SIEM alerts into incident-level
  communities, extracts behavioural subject-relation-target triples from each
  community under a grammar-constrained decoder, and uses a knowledge graph
  bridge into MITRE ATT&CK to restrict which techniques retrieval may return.
  Anchoring retrieval in extracted behaviour converts an open-domain search
  over 691 technique descriptions into a closed-set choice among candidates the
  observed evidence supports. Runs entirely on local hardware within 4 GB of
  video memory.
keywords:
  - security operations
  - MITRE ATT&CK
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - knowledge graphs
  - large language models
  - incident response
  - SIEM
license: Apache-2.0
